<figure class="markov-comparison">
  <div
    class="comparison-frame"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="markov-comparison-title markov-comparison-description"
  >
    <div class="comparison-intro">
      <p class="comparison-kicker">The test</p>
      <h3 id="markov-comparison-title">Does history change the prediction?</h3>
    </div>

    <p id="markov-comparison-description" class="sr-only">
      Two diagrams compare different histories that arrive at the same current
      representation and action. In the non-Markovian representation, the histories lead
      to different predictions for the next representation and reward. In the Markovian
      representation, both histories lead to the same prediction because the
      current state already contains every relevant fact from the past.
    </p>

    <div class="comparison-panels" aria-hidden="true">
      <section class="comparison-panel comparison-panel-broken">
        <header>
          <span class="status-mark">×</span>
          <span>
            <small>History still matters</small>
            <strong>Not Markovian</strong>
          </span>
        </header>

        <svg viewBox="0 0 360 348">
          <defs>
            <marker id="broken-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
              <path d="M0 0 10 5 0 10Z" />
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <text class="micro-label" x="180" y="25" text-anchor="middle">TWO DIFFERENT HISTORIES</text>

          <g class="history history-one">
            <rect x="40" y="42" width="112" height="36" rx="18" />
            <text x="96" y="65" text-anchor="middle">z₀  ·  a₀  ·  r₁  ·  …</text>
            <text class="history-label" x="27" y="65">H₁</text>
          </g>
          <g class="history history-two">
            <rect x="208" y="42" width="112" height="36" rx="18" />
            <text x="264" y="65" text-anchor="middle">z₀  ·  a₀  ·  r₁  ·  …</text>
            <text class="history-label" x="333" y="65">H₂</text>
          </g>

          <path class="history-path" d="M96 79 C96 111 144 111 164 132" />
          <path class="history-path" d="M264 79 C264 111 216 111 196 132" />

          <g class="present-state">
            <rect x="126" y="124" width="108" height="54" rx="14" />
            <text class="box-label" x="180" y="145" text-anchor="middle">CURRENT INPUT</text>
            <text class="math-label" x="180" y="166" text-anchor="middle">zₜ</text>
          </g>

          <path class="flow-path" d="M180 179 V207" marker-end="url(#broken-arrow)" />
          <g class="action-node">
            <rect x="148" y="211" width="64" height="34" rx="17" />
            <text x="180" y="233" text-anchor="middle">action aₜ</text>
          </g>

          <path class="broken-path" d="M180 246 V260 C180 274 112 271 97 286" marker-end="url(#broken-arrow)" />
          <path class="broken-path" d="M180 246 V260 C180 274 248 271 263 286" marker-end="url(#broken-arrow)" />

          <g class="outcome outcome-one">
            <rect x="39" y="291" width="116" height="40" rx="12" />
            <text x="97" y="316" text-anchor="middle">prediction 1</text>
          </g>
          <g class="outcome outcome-two">
            <rect x="205" y="291" width="116" height="40" rx="12" />
            <text x="263" y="316" text-anchor="middle">prediction 2</text>
          </g>
          <text class="history-decides" x="180" y="344" text-anchor="middle">H changes what comes next</text>
        </svg>

        <p class="panel-equation">p(z′, r | z, a, H) ≠ p(z′, r | z, a)</p>
      </section>

      <section class="comparison-panel comparison-panel-valid">
        <header>
          <span class="status-mark">✓</span>
          <span>
            <small>History adds nothing</small>
            <strong>Markovian</strong>
          </span>
        </header>

        <svg viewBox="0 0 360 348">
          <defs>
            <marker id="valid-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
              <path d="M0 0 10 5 0 10Z" />
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <text class="micro-label" x="180" y="25" text-anchor="middle">TWO DIFFERENT HISTORIES</text>

          <g class="history history-one">
            <rect x="40" y="42" width="112" height="36" rx="18" />
            <text x="96" y="65" text-anchor="middle">z₀  ·  a₀  ·  r₁  ·  …</text>
            <text class="history-label" x="27" y="65">H₁</text>
          </g>
          <g class="history history-two">
            <rect x="208" y="42" width="112" height="36" rx="18" />
            <text x="264" y="65" text-anchor="middle">z₀  ·  a₀  ·  r₁  ·  …</text>
            <text class="history-label" x="333" y="65">H₂</text>
          </g>

          <path class="history-path" d="M96 79 C96 111 144 111 164 132" />
          <path class="history-path" d="M264 79 C264 111 216 111 196 132" />

          <g class="present-state">
            <rect x="126" y="124" width="108" height="54" rx="14" />
            <text class="box-label" x="180" y="145" text-anchor="middle">CURRENT INPUT</text>
            <text class="math-label" x="180" y="166" text-anchor="middle">zₜ</text>
          </g>

          <text class="state-note" x="248" y="149">holds every</text>
          <text class="state-note" x="248" y="164">relevant fact</text>

          <path class="flow-path" d="M180 179 V207" marker-end="url(#valid-arrow)" />
          <g class="action-node">
            <rect x="148" y="211" width="64" height="34" rx="17" />
            <text x="180" y="233" text-anchor="middle">action aₜ</text>
          </g>

          <path class="valid-path" d="M180 246 V286" marker-end="url(#valid-arrow)" />
          <g class="outcome outcome-shared">
            <rect x="111" y="291" width="138" height="40" rx="12" />
            <text x="180" y="316" text-anchor="middle">same prediction</text>
          </g>
          <text class="history-irrelevant" x="180" y="344" text-anchor="middle">H cannot change what comes next</text>
        </svg>

        <p class="panel-equation">p(z′, r | z, a, H) = p(z′, r | z, a)</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    The test is not whether the histories differ. It is whether knowing which
    history occurred changes the predicted next state or reward after the
    current representation and action are already known.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

